On 2007-01-09, azgor wrote:
>
> [2]: Is it possible to bury a wand of digging? If so, it should refuse
> to allow itself to be buried, unless it has been cancelled. This should
> break the boulder instead of filling the pit. --BenUrban

This kind of "intelligent" behaviour would be unusual and unfitting for 
profane objects. And yes, there is the engraving effect of the wand of
striking, but that's more YAFM than anything else.

> [3]: Decorative objects. Objects you can't interact with much but that
> give the game a more immersive/realistic feel. The occasional skeleton.
> Sarcophagi. Rubble in the corner. Broken arrows. Shafts of light from
> above. Mist. --azgor

I'd rather keep it simple. No objects that don't add to gameplay in some
way. And how do you imagine shafts of light and mist, especially in ASCII?

> [4]: Djinnis should cross their arms, blink, and nod as they grant your
> wish as per the TV show. --azgor

YAFM? Well, if you like.

> [5]: An uncursed ring of levitation hits the ceiling, then falls back
> on top of your head. <-- that ring should hover for a moment, or
> something --BenUrban

See [2].

> [6]: Vomiting should wipe out any text written in the dust. --muumiponi

Should it? Dropping anything else on the floor doesn't.

> [7]: Ethereal monsters, such as barrow wights, shouldn't be able to get
> caught in bear traps. --TheShrewdDude

The beartrap code currently checks for the monster properties "amorphous",
"whirly" and "unsolid". Barrow wights are considered neither, while wraiths
are considered unsolid. I'd suspect that's intentional.

> [9]: When doing multiple searches (<number>s), and you find a hidden
> door or pathway, give a message ("You find a hidden door/whatever! You
> stop searching."), instead of just stopping the search. --Chilliwack

The door or pathway appears on the screen. That's enough info for me.

> [11]: To reward uber-fast ascensions, how about something like 10
> points for every turn under 20000 turns? (adjust numbers to make them
> come out right) --Yui

Just adjusting the current score system with a "cosmological constant"-like
factor to correct its bias seems wrong. I'd rather see a completely new
score system that assesses a game in a more-than-one dimensional score
space. (And the cosmologists can keep their mouths shut about the validity
of a cosmological constant. I'll believe the theory of the week when it's
been undisputed for a century or two.)

> [13]: When things "wear" a shield, it says they put it on... don't you,
> like, hold a shield, or strap it to your arm? Maybe a message more
> appropriate would be appropriate. --Chilliwack

Usually there's a strap around your arm beneath the elbow and a second
strap you hold in your hand. I think that can be described as "wearing"
just as well as, say, wearing a ring can.

> [14]: At game end, also report the number of times the player prayed
> (to each god). --Yui
>
> [15]: At game end, also report the number of times the player
> sacrificed. --Yui

Who'd want to know? Atheism is already reported. "Not prayed more than n
times" where n>0 seems a rather arbitrary conduct.

> [18]: It should be possible to gain some intrinsics by eating various
> articles of clothing -- e.g. (as a gelatinous cube) eating an elven
> cloak would have a chance of granting stealth. It would be interesting
> to see intrinsic displacement... --Yui

Why not. If you can gain intrinsics from eating rings, magical armor seems
a logical continuation of that. Be sure not to introduce too many new
intrinsics, or the choice of armor to wear would be made easier and thus
more boring.

> [19]: According to http://hea-www.harvard.edu/~fine/Fun/polearms.html ,
> all the stats for the polearms should be revisited, including damage,
> weight, etc. --Yui

NHINRL. Weights and damage rates of weapons should be aproximately
consistent with reality, but game balance considerations trump that.

> [20]: When listing intrinsics at the end of the game, change "You were
> protected" to "You were protected (+5)" or whatever, to show the
> improvement in naked AC. --Yui

Why not.


